    "evidence": "Composer passes automated WCAG checks at all three viewports, all 10 controls are keyboard-reachable with visible focus, no touch-target violations or viewport overflow were measured, and reduced-motion sampling found no changed elements. However, header contrast remains unresolved: axe reports 12 serious color-contrast incomplete nodes on mobile and one on tablet. Touch-target evidence covers #composer only, not the global header. The mobile/tablet navigation is clipped into a contained horizontal scroller, so it avoids document overflow but still lacks measured touch and scroll-accessibility proof.",
